1
00:00:00,227 --> 00:00:06,009
FILING FOR LOVE

2
00:01:29,884 --> 00:01:33,261
EPISODE 5:
HEART BURN

3
00:01:52,925 --> 00:01:54,301
{\an8}Miss.

4
00:01:55,803 --> 00:01:57,263
{\an8}My heart was burning.

5
00:01:59,432 --> 00:02:00,641
{\an8}I'm ready to pay.

6
00:02:00,725 --> 00:02:02,101
{\an8}SOJU

7
00:02:02,184 --> 00:02:03,644
{\an8}Miss.

8
00:02:03,728 --> 00:02:05,693
{\an8}You'll die if you drink all this.

9
00:02:06,173 --> 00:02:07,215
That's the plan.

10
00:02:07,299 --> 00:02:09,885
Did something bad happen?

11
00:02:16,475 --> 00:02:17,809
I don't know

12
00:02:19,061 --> 00:02:20,437
what's happening.

13
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:33,408
Hey, are you okay?
You're alive in there, right?

14
00:02:34,201 --> 00:02:35,994
How many hours
do you need to shower for?

15
00:02:58,892 --> 00:03:00,686
You could end up getting dehydrated.

16
00:03:05,315 --> 00:03:06,608
I'd like a beer, too.

17
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:16,326
Why are you so flushed?

18
00:03:17,035 --> 00:03:18,578
Are you unwell?

19
00:03:18,995 --> 00:03:19,996
Is it a fever?

20
00:03:21,039 --> 00:03:22,624
You don't feel hot.

21
00:03:26,712 --> 00:03:27,879
I shouldn't flirt.

22
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,716
I can't have you falling for me.

23
00:03:32,092 --> 00:03:33,844
Can it really happen?

24
00:03:34,386 --> 00:03:35,971
Can you really fall for someone

25
00:03:36,263 --> 00:03:38,724
you've known for so long?
Like you were hit by lightning.

26
00:03:38,807 --> 00:03:40,308
Did you really fall for me?

27
00:03:40,392 --> 00:03:42,310
That's only possible
if I were struck by lightning.

28
00:03:45,605 --> 00:03:47,441
Of course, it's possible.

29
00:03:48,108 --> 00:03:51,236
If you're given a reason
to see the person in a new light.

30
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:54,698
Or it's possible
you'd already fallen for them.

31
00:03:55,365 --> 00:03:58,410
Before you knew it,
all your built-up feelings about them

32
00:03:58,493 --> 00:04:02,080
just blow up in an instant

33
00:04:02,748 --> 00:04:03,874
like lava.

34
00:04:05,459 --> 00:04:06,793
Like lava.

35
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:10,714
J CONVALESCENT HOSPITAL

36
00:04:16,052 --> 00:04:17,137
Mother.

37
00:04:19,639 --> 00:04:20,974
The people here.

38
00:04:22,225 --> 00:04:24,060
They're not harassing you.

39
00:04:25,395 --> 00:04:26,730
They want to help you.

40
00:04:28,482 --> 00:04:30,609
If you refuse your medicine
and cause a fuss

41
00:04:32,444 --> 00:04:34,154
they'll send you back
to the psych ward.

42
00:04:42,829 --> 00:04:45,040
FATHER

43
00:04:52,714 --> 00:04:53,965
- Hello, Father.
<i>- Where are you?</i>

44
00:04:55,133 --> 00:04:56,384
I'm exercising.

45
00:04:56,468 --> 00:04:58,720
<i>You have time for that?
What are you up to?</i>

46
00:04:59,179 --> 00:05:01,306
You hired a fool like that
for that much money?

47
00:05:01,765 --> 00:05:03,683
If you did,
you must've put him to good use!

48
00:05:03,767 --> 00:05:05,060
<i>Why did you cause trouble?</i>

49
00:05:05,936 --> 00:05:06,978
HAEMU FIRES LOCKETT
FOR SEXUAL MISCONDUCT

50
00:05:07,062 --> 00:05:08,188
<i>The Audit Team went after him.</i>

51
00:05:08,396 --> 00:05:10,398
<i>You still don't have control
of your own people?</i>

52
00:05:10,857 --> 00:05:12,943
<i>Who do you take after
to be this weak?</i>

53
00:05:13,151 --> 00:05:14,820
<i>Think about who you are
and what you are.</i>

54
00:05:14,986 --> 00:05:17,072
<i>If you can't handle it,
you'll crumble, just like your mom.</i>

55
00:05:35,507 --> 00:05:37,175
Starting today, I want Joo In-a

56
00:05:37,759 --> 00:05:39,010
included in the executive updates.

57
00:05:39,094 --> 00:05:40,637
The Audit Team
keeps tabs on executives

58
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,515
and report regularly,
so the Head isn't included in...

59
00:05:47,352 --> 00:05:48,603
I understand, sir.

60
00:05:48,687 --> 00:05:50,856
We'll keep tabs on her ourselves.

61
00:06:19,926 --> 00:06:21,386
Hello, Ms. Joo.

62
00:06:22,053 --> 00:06:23,555
Yes, hello. How are you?

63
00:06:23,889 --> 00:06:26,224
It was a pity
you missed the team dinner.

64
00:06:26,558 --> 00:06:29,185
It was.
Let's hope there's a next time.

65
00:06:29,311 --> 00:06:30,353
How about

66
00:06:30,854 --> 00:06:33,106
you and I grab a drink?

67
00:06:33,189 --> 00:06:34,608
Just you and me.

68
00:06:37,819 --> 00:06:40,280
I don't see how you'd enjoy
joining me for a drink.

69
00:06:40,530 --> 00:06:41,698
We have nothing in common.

70
00:06:41,781 --> 00:06:43,491
There might be something.

71
00:06:43,867 --> 00:06:47,287
You and I could have
something surprising in common.

72
00:07:23,823 --> 00:07:25,075
Morning.

73
00:07:25,367 --> 00:07:28,078
Let's have a coffee.
We need to talk, too.

74
00:07:29,955 --> 00:07:31,039
Forget the coffee.

75
00:07:31,623 --> 00:07:33,416
We can talk in the interview room.

76
00:08:16,626 --> 00:08:18,837
- Yesterday...
- Sorry about that. I apologize.

77
00:08:19,921 --> 00:08:22,215
I shouldn't have done that
as your superior.

78
00:08:23,091 --> 00:08:24,843
If you want to lodge
an official complaint

79
00:08:25,552 --> 00:08:26,553
then go ahead.

80
00:08:27,012 --> 00:08:28,847
I'll admit and accept everything.

81
00:08:31,141 --> 00:08:33,351
You seem to be gravely mistaken.

82
00:08:34,561 --> 00:08:35,895
I kissed you.

83
00:08:37,647 --> 00:08:39,983
What are you talking about?
I'm the one who kissed you.

84
00:08:40,066 --> 00:08:42,277
I kissed you, Ms. Joo.

85
00:08:42,652 --> 00:08:44,195
Don't argue with me. I started it.

86
00:08:44,279 --> 00:08:46,531
I'm not arguing.
Do you think you used

87
00:08:46,614 --> 00:08:47,949
your rank or authority
to pressure me?

88
00:08:49,367 --> 00:08:51,870
Why are you trying to subdue me?

89
00:08:51,953 --> 00:08:53,830
- I'm saying I did what I did.
- I did it.

90
00:08:53,913 --> 00:08:55,915
- I did it.
- Why?

91
00:08:59,753 --> 00:09:01,337
Why did you kiss me?

92
00:09:02,338 --> 00:09:03,590
That is, if you did it.

93
00:09:06,718 --> 00:09:07,761
I was intoxicated

94
00:09:08,553 --> 00:09:09,637
with art.

95
00:09:10,055 --> 00:09:12,974
You're a great artist.
Your work was just beautiful.

96
00:09:13,058 --> 00:09:16,102
Not to mention the calm music
playing in the background.

97
00:09:16,186 --> 00:09:18,521
There was something about the moment
and its atmosphere.

98
00:09:19,189 --> 00:09:20,398
It was intoxicating.

99
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:22,067
There's a scientific rationale.

100
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:24,861
A great work of art
stimulates dopamine secretion

101
00:09:24,944 --> 00:09:27,781
which arouses you,
accelerating your pulse and breath.

102
00:09:29,866 --> 00:09:31,201
Like you're under a magic spell.

103
00:09:40,335 --> 00:09:41,961
Was what I drew that good?

104
00:09:42,754 --> 00:09:44,589
Do you think
I'm Michelangelo or something?

105
00:09:45,423 --> 00:09:47,509
I should call you Noh-chelangelo.

106
00:09:50,845 --> 00:09:53,056
The excuse you came up with
was that art intoxicated you?

107
00:09:53,181 --> 00:09:54,265
That's all there is to it?

108
00:09:55,892 --> 00:09:57,185
What about you, then?

109
00:09:57,435 --> 00:09:59,813
Why did you kiss me?
That is, if you did it first.

110
00:10:04,818 --> 00:10:05,902
You were pretty.

111
00:10:07,946 --> 00:10:10,156
I was stone-cold sober
and in my right mind.

112
00:10:10,990 --> 00:10:12,659
I just found you pretty.

113
00:10:15,411 --> 00:10:16,538
That's why I kissed you.

114
00:10:26,923 --> 00:10:28,091
I've always been pretty.

115
00:10:29,676 --> 00:10:31,553
Anyone would say so.
I have nice facial features

116
00:10:31,636 --> 00:10:33,012
and they're in the right place.

117
00:10:33,096 --> 00:10:34,222
I have an objectively pretty face.

118
00:10:34,639 --> 00:10:35,723
So what?

119
00:10:36,141 --> 00:10:38,476
That doesn't mean
every man kisses me.

120
00:10:44,482 --> 00:10:45,733
Regardless of who started it

121
00:10:46,234 --> 00:10:49,154
we have to admit what happened
yesterday wasn't normal.

122
00:10:49,946 --> 00:10:51,489
To make sure
this doesn't happen again

123
00:10:51,573 --> 00:10:54,284
let's keep a reasonable distance
for risk management purposes.

124
00:10:54,367 --> 00:10:56,786
We should keep our work
and private lives separate, too. Bye.

125
00:11:05,378 --> 00:11:08,047
Just so you know,
it's really annoying.

126
00:11:09,507 --> 00:11:10,758
Kissing and then apologizing for it.

127
00:11:18,224 --> 00:11:20,476
Mr. Cha, born in 1988,
Year of the Dragon.

128
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,145
Your daily fortune says...

129
00:11:22,937 --> 00:11:25,732
Oh, you should organize
your surroundings.

130
00:11:25,815 --> 00:11:29,319
Hae-young, born in 1989,
Year of the Snake.

131
00:11:30,987 --> 00:11:33,615
Gosh. Someone special
will come from the west.

132
00:11:33,865 --> 00:11:35,325
- The west?
- Ms. Pyun.

133
00:11:35,617 --> 00:11:37,160
I live in Bucheon in the west.

134
00:11:37,952 --> 00:11:39,037
Am I special to you?

135
00:11:40,038 --> 00:11:42,874
Mr. Moo with the Year of the Ram.

136
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:46,836
Try not to get noticed
by your superior.

137
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,338
- My superior?
- Your superior.

138
00:11:50,882 --> 00:11:52,008
Where is she?

139
00:11:53,051 --> 00:11:54,886
- What's up?
- Shoot.

140
00:11:55,386 --> 00:11:57,847
Oh, dear, gosh.

141
00:11:58,223 --> 00:11:59,891
The economy has changed a great deal.

142
00:11:59,974 --> 00:12:02,352
What's the world coming to?

143
00:12:03,686 --> 00:12:06,105
What do you think is up
with those two this morning?

144
00:12:06,189 --> 00:12:08,483
Mr. Noh has always been
in Ms. Joo's bad books.

145
00:12:08,566 --> 00:12:11,152
I thought things had improved
while working on James's case.

146
00:12:11,236 --> 00:12:12,904
What if things
go really badly for Mr. Noh

147
00:12:13,404 --> 00:12:14,989
and chaos comes for him?

148
00:12:15,073 --> 00:12:18,701
I have a feeling we should step up
and help him out

149
00:12:18,785 --> 00:12:21,412
so the two can get closer.
Oh, my gosh.

150
00:12:21,496 --> 00:12:24,874
Oh, dear. AI.
Artificial Intelligence...

151
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:26,334
It's just...

152
00:12:33,883 --> 00:12:35,468
I'm so jealous of him.

153
00:12:35,927 --> 00:12:37,720
This is his lucky year.

154
00:12:37,804 --> 00:12:41,349
He got married and was named
Haemu Cosmetics' King of Sales.

155
00:12:41,474 --> 00:12:43,851
It's not the first time
he won that title.

156
00:12:44,269 --> 00:12:45,603
The punk.

157
00:12:45,853 --> 00:12:48,439
I begged him to share
his trade secret, but he won't.

158
00:12:48,523 --> 00:12:51,025
- Let's go outside for a smoke.
- Sure.

159
00:13:14,799 --> 00:13:16,342
Are you all ready?

160
00:13:16,426 --> 00:13:18,886
One, two, three.

161
00:13:32,942 --> 00:13:34,235
What the heck's going on?

162
00:13:34,944 --> 00:13:35,987
What is she doing?

163
00:13:36,654 --> 00:13:37,697
Hands off me!

164
00:13:44,162 --> 00:13:47,498
I have no relationship whatsoever
with that woman.

165
00:13:48,166 --> 00:13:50,960
She's the head buyer
at one of our clients.

166
00:13:51,044 --> 00:13:52,795
I'm a salesman at her mercy.

167
00:13:52,879 --> 00:13:54,589
She's the buyer in control.

168
00:13:55,256 --> 00:13:56,341
That's it.

169
00:13:56,424 --> 00:13:59,719
But she caused a ruckus
at your wedding for no good reason?

170
00:13:59,802 --> 00:14:00,970
Exactly.

171
00:14:01,054 --> 00:14:03,556
How confused and rattled
do you think I was?

172
00:14:03,848 --> 00:14:06,726
If we had even a situationship,
I wouldn't have invited her.

173
00:14:06,809 --> 00:14:08,269
I'm not that crazy.

174
00:14:09,854 --> 00:14:11,439
Bros, this is totally unfair.

175
00:14:11,522 --> 00:14:13,608
We're not your bros, Mr. Do.

176
00:14:14,108 --> 00:14:16,694
Sit up straight.
We're not here to fool around.

177
00:14:17,028 --> 00:14:18,279
Sorry.

178
00:14:18,696 --> 00:14:20,656
Anyway,
there really isn't much to it.

179
00:14:21,574 --> 00:14:23,618
That's why even after that disaster
at my wedding

180
00:14:23,868 --> 00:14:25,411
I'm enjoying my newlywed life.

181
00:14:25,745 --> 00:14:28,623
There must be a reason she acted out.

182
00:14:29,123 --> 00:14:31,793
Did you give her reason to think
there was something between you?

183
00:14:35,671 --> 00:14:36,714
Well, actually...

184
00:14:37,548 --> 00:14:39,884
I've actually got
a sales tactic of my own.

185
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:44,263
I sell lipsticks for a living.

186
00:14:44,472 --> 00:14:46,182
Most of the buyers are women.

187
00:14:46,265 --> 00:14:48,935
When a man and a woman work together

188
00:14:49,018 --> 00:14:51,229
there's bound to be
a little sexual chemistry.

189
00:14:51,312 --> 00:14:54,023
I use that as best I can
to make a sale.

190
00:14:54,357 --> 00:14:57,610
Are you saying you get your way
by using your physique somehow?

191
00:14:57,985 --> 00:15:01,072
Gosh, no, bro... Mr. Cha.

192
00:15:03,699 --> 00:15:05,576
Flirting. That's it.

193
00:15:05,827 --> 00:15:08,746
One, do just enough. Two, be polite.

194
00:15:08,830 --> 00:15:11,874
But how? You make the lady feel good.

195
00:15:12,333 --> 00:15:14,627
You create a thrill and tension.

196
00:15:14,710 --> 00:15:17,755
I prey on their emotions
without crossing the line.

197
00:15:18,714 --> 00:15:21,342
They usually know what's happening
and play along.

198
00:15:22,385 --> 00:15:24,971
Is Ms. So a bit delusional?

199
00:15:28,224 --> 00:15:29,934
We were definitely dating.

200
00:15:33,396 --> 00:15:36,482
You don't have to say,
"We're now officially together."

201
00:15:36,732 --> 00:15:39,068
There comes a moment
when you just know

202
00:15:39,485 --> 00:15:41,320
that you have something special.

203
00:15:41,446 --> 00:15:42,905
I was confused at first.

204
00:15:42,989 --> 00:15:45,992
I thought he was being nice
just to increase his sales.

205
00:15:53,332 --> 00:15:55,793
Oh, dear. Are you that ill?

206
00:15:55,877 --> 00:15:58,337
<i>I said I was unwell, and he brought
porridge and medicine</i>

207
00:15:58,421 --> 00:16:00,006
<i>in the middle of the night.</i>

208
00:16:00,882 --> 00:16:04,177
<i>That's something you do
when you actually care about someone.</i>

209
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:05,511
Dress warmly.

210
00:16:05,595 --> 00:16:07,555
Yes, that's usually true.

211
00:16:07,638 --> 00:16:08,681
But in that case...

212
00:16:09,474 --> 00:16:12,268
<i>I needed her to settle the bill,
and she said she was too sick.</i>

213
00:16:12,852 --> 00:16:15,021
<i>What else could I do
but try to make her feel better?</i>

214
00:16:16,022 --> 00:16:19,233
<i>I went to a nearby pharmacy
and bought all the strongest meds.</i>

215
00:16:19,317 --> 00:16:21,194
- This must be taken warm.
- That, too?

216
00:16:21,277 --> 00:16:22,361
<i>She loved the attention.</i>

217
00:16:22,445 --> 00:16:24,906
<i>- She wired the money the next day.</i>
- Get well soon.

218
00:16:26,616 --> 00:16:29,160
<i>So I accepted his date request.</i>

219
00:16:30,161 --> 00:16:32,914
- Hello.
<i>- We watched a movie and ate out.</i>

220
00:16:33,331 --> 00:16:35,208
<i>It was an ordinary weekend date.</i>

221
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,586
<i>A date?
So that's what she thought it was.</i>

222
00:16:40,254 --> 00:16:43,508
<i>"I'm bored on weekends.
I roll around at home all day long."</i>

223
00:16:43,591 --> 00:16:46,385
<i>She kept whining, so I sent her
movie tickets the company gives us.</i>

224
00:16:46,469 --> 00:16:48,095
<i>When she got them...</i>

225
00:16:48,846 --> 00:16:50,473
<i>She said she was only free
that Saturday.</i>

226
00:16:50,556 --> 00:16:53,601
<i>It felt like I was going to work
on a weekend.</i>

227
00:16:54,393 --> 00:16:55,728
<i>"Going to work"?</i>

228
00:16:56,521 --> 00:16:59,440
<i>He never stopped saying
I was cute or pretty</i>

229
00:17:00,149 --> 00:17:03,152
<i>and wiped my lips
when I got food on my face.</i>

230
00:17:04,278 --> 00:17:05,613
<i>Is that part of his job description?</i>

231
00:17:08,157 --> 00:17:09,283
Take a look.

232
00:17:11,327 --> 00:17:14,705
He texts me, "Good morning"
and "Good night"

233
00:17:14,789 --> 00:17:16,415
every single day without fail.

234
00:17:17,375 --> 00:17:18,876
And this means nothing?

235
00:17:19,794 --> 00:17:22,380
Let us take a look at that.

236
00:17:23,381 --> 00:17:24,632
Let's scroll up.

237
00:17:26,133 --> 00:17:27,760
OKAY, I'LL EMAIL IT TO YOU!

238
00:17:27,843 --> 00:17:29,095
GOOD NIGHT, SEE YOU TOMORROW

239
00:17:30,763 --> 00:17:32,139
I see your point.

240
00:17:33,849 --> 00:17:34,892
Thanks.

241
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,019
The thing is...

242
00:17:38,062 --> 00:17:39,981
We checked Mr. Do's phone as well.

243
00:17:41,148 --> 00:17:43,859
He texts the same thing
to all his clients.

244
00:17:44,318 --> 00:17:46,487
It's practically copied and pasted.

245
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:49,198
Copied and pasted?

246
00:17:50,908 --> 00:17:52,118
He's a psycho.

247
00:17:52,201 --> 00:17:55,496
Do you have another clearer incident

248
00:17:55,955 --> 00:17:59,041
that could help
prove your relationship?

249
00:18:02,295 --> 00:18:03,462
The kiss.

250
00:18:05,423 --> 00:18:07,258
He and I kissed.

251
00:18:08,301 --> 00:18:09,510
"Kiss"?

252
00:18:12,263 --> 00:18:14,765
This is just madness.

253
00:18:15,391 --> 00:18:18,185
I'm a guy who never crosses a line.

254
00:18:18,519 --> 00:18:20,396
Physical touch? Never.

255
00:18:20,479 --> 00:18:22,106
You brought her medicine at night

256
00:18:22,189 --> 00:18:23,858
went to a movie together
and texted each other

257
00:18:24,233 --> 00:18:27,069
- but you didn't kiss?
- We didn't. Never.

258
00:18:33,242 --> 00:18:35,494
Why did you stop the investigation
halfway through?

259
00:18:35,870 --> 00:18:38,122
You called a client over
for questioning

260
00:18:38,706 --> 00:18:40,166
and you don't conclude your report?

261
00:18:40,249 --> 00:18:42,877
It's a personal issue
between the two of them.

262
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:45,254
They have different opinions
about one incident.

263
00:18:45,338 --> 00:18:47,089
How can we check that objectively?

264
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:49,091
Don't you know the saying

265
00:18:49,175 --> 00:18:51,844
the truth between two people
isn't with just one

266
00:18:51,969 --> 00:18:53,638
but it exists
on the periphery of both.

267
00:18:53,721 --> 00:18:55,848
Then you must check the periphery.

268
00:18:55,931 --> 00:18:57,850
They clearly disagree on one matter.

269
00:18:57,933 --> 00:19:00,102
Ms. So says they kissed.
Mr. Do says they didn't.

270
00:19:00,186 --> 00:19:01,479
Isn't that an important point?

271
00:19:02,605 --> 00:19:05,107
If Mr. Do is denying kissing her

272
00:19:05,191 --> 00:19:08,110
that could be sexual harassment,
and it could hurt business ties.

273
00:19:08,235 --> 00:19:10,780
Not to mention
it's incredibly rude to the lady.

274
00:19:13,407 --> 00:19:14,742
I see.

275
00:19:15,576 --> 00:19:17,411
Is that how important a kiss is?

276
00:19:19,538 --> 00:19:20,873
Even after the kiss

277
00:19:22,458 --> 00:19:24,710
I thought an apology
would settle everything.

278
00:19:30,216 --> 00:19:31,634
Let's stick to work.

279
00:19:33,177 --> 00:19:34,387
Where did they kiss?

280
00:19:39,892 --> 00:19:41,644
It was after they ate here.

281
00:19:45,606 --> 00:19:47,608
Describe the situation in detail.

282
00:19:47,692 --> 00:19:49,860
Do your job properly, Mr. Noh.

283
00:20:02,164 --> 00:20:05,292
They left after having
a few cocktails at the bar upstairs.

284
00:20:05,376 --> 00:20:08,129
Ms. So can't drink much,
so she was very drunk.

285
00:20:08,212 --> 00:20:10,005
She could barely walk.

286
00:20:10,339 --> 00:20:11,507
And then...

287
00:20:23,018 --> 00:20:24,562
I feel dizzy.

288
00:20:26,021 --> 00:20:27,064
Oh, my gosh.

289
00:20:29,150 --> 00:20:32,695
So Mr. Do helped Ms. So
stand up straight.

290
00:20:36,490 --> 00:20:38,159
They stood here, facing each other.

291
00:20:54,258 --> 00:20:56,093
There's no need
to reenact the whole thing.

292
00:20:56,343 --> 00:20:57,887
You told me to go into detail.

293
00:20:57,970 --> 00:20:59,263
You're contradicting yourself.

294
00:21:02,892 --> 00:21:04,894
There's a camera up there.
Let's get the footage.

295
00:21:05,603 --> 00:21:07,146
It looks like a fake.

296
00:21:10,691 --> 00:21:11,692
How can you tell?

297
00:21:12,026 --> 00:21:13,068
Look carefully.

298
00:21:14,153 --> 00:21:16,155
There are no electrical wires

299
00:21:16,405 --> 00:21:17,573
or blinking light.

300
00:21:19,450 --> 00:21:20,785
It's cold to the touch.

301
00:21:21,243 --> 00:21:23,162
I bet it never worked.

302
00:21:23,579 --> 00:21:26,832
Hey, Mr. Noh. You have your uses.

303
00:21:34,548 --> 00:21:36,926
There should be a camera or two here.

304
00:21:44,767 --> 00:21:46,101
ROTISSERIE CHICKEN

305
00:21:56,542 --> 00:21:59,378
So, did the DOJ meeting happen?

306
00:22:00,223 --> 00:22:02,183
I heard JB pulled some strings.

307
00:22:02,267 --> 00:22:03,768
You jerk.

308
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:06,729
You invited me out to practice
just to discuss work?

309
00:22:10,275 --> 00:22:13,528
Sir. It's Managing Director Jeon.
What shall I do?

310
00:22:13,611 --> 00:22:15,697
- Say I'll call him back.
- Yes, sir.

311
00:22:23,246 --> 00:22:25,373
Isn't she a looker? Can you focus?

312
00:22:25,457 --> 00:22:27,542
She's smart and thorough.

313
00:22:27,625 --> 00:22:28,960
You're so uptight.

314
00:22:29,043 --> 00:22:31,212
I understand.

315
00:22:31,588 --> 00:22:33,715
You need someone to talk to.

316
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:38,887
I get that your marriage was
a business deal, but your wife...

317
00:22:40,638 --> 00:22:42,724
I couldn't live with her
even if my dad threatened to kill me.

318
00:22:48,813 --> 00:22:51,024
- Hello, sir.
- Hi there.

319
00:22:51,107 --> 00:22:52,859
The chicken looks amazing.

320
00:22:52,942 --> 00:22:56,029
They're so plump, I thought
they were turkeys from over there.

321
00:22:56,779 --> 00:22:58,323
They taste just as good, too.

322
00:22:58,406 --> 00:23:01,117
Mr. Noh. Isn't it mesmerizing
to watch them turn?

323
00:23:01,201 --> 00:23:03,703
I wish I could do that to you
whenever you get on my nerves.

324
00:23:04,662 --> 00:23:06,372
Oh, you like to truss people up?

325
00:23:09,667 --> 00:23:12,754
Sir, how many times a week
do you come here?

326
00:23:12,837 --> 00:23:14,881
I'm here every day apart from Sunday.

327
00:23:14,964 --> 00:23:16,216
Oh, really?

328
00:23:16,716 --> 00:23:21,054
Do you park your truck
at this angle whenever you're here?

329
00:23:22,388 --> 00:23:23,515
What?

330
00:23:23,598 --> 00:23:27,227
Do you park your truck
like this every time?

331
00:23:31,147 --> 00:23:33,441
It smells amazing.

332
00:23:33,525 --> 00:23:36,110
Take this home
and share with your family.

333
00:23:36,194 --> 00:23:37,403
You have a big family.

334
00:23:37,487 --> 00:23:40,073
We live separately now.

335
00:23:40,156 --> 00:23:42,075
Do you live on your own, then?

336
00:23:42,534 --> 00:23:43,576
Yes.

337
00:23:51,459 --> 00:23:52,544
Hello?

338
00:23:57,257 --> 00:23:58,800
You got the wrong number.

339
00:24:06,182 --> 00:24:07,475
Who was that?

340
00:24:08,226 --> 00:24:09,477
A wrong number.

341
00:24:10,895 --> 00:24:12,146
Let's take a look.

342
00:24:13,022 --> 00:24:14,732
We got the perfect angle.

343
00:24:14,816 --> 00:24:16,025
Press rewind.

344
00:24:16,568 --> 00:24:17,860
We must go back

345
00:24:18,570 --> 00:24:20,822
to between 10 p.m. and midnight.

346
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:25,076
There they are.

347
00:24:47,432 --> 00:24:49,559
Gosh, they actually kissed.

348
00:25:01,654 --> 00:25:04,157
Mr. Choi got a call
that his second kid was hurt.

349
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,617
I told him to go home.

350
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:08,119
Good for you. Tell him to take
as long as he needs off work.

351
00:25:08,202 --> 00:25:09,412
Yes, sir.

352
00:25:10,079 --> 00:25:11,706
I'll drive you home tonight.

353
00:25:13,583 --> 00:25:15,668
It's fine. I'll drive.

354
00:25:21,049 --> 00:25:22,133
Bye, then.

355
00:25:26,512 --> 00:25:27,513
Ms. Park.

356
00:25:31,768 --> 00:25:33,061
Where did you move to?

357
00:25:52,622 --> 00:25:54,165
You can drop me off here.

358
00:26:01,673 --> 00:26:02,799
Thank you, sir.

359
00:26:04,425 --> 00:26:05,510
Ms. Park.

360
00:26:06,094 --> 00:26:07,720
From now on, Mr. Choi or Do-young

361
00:26:08,346 --> 00:26:10,139
will accompany me
on my personal business.

362
00:26:10,765 --> 00:26:13,351
I'd like you to concentrate
on work-related tasks.

363
00:26:18,147 --> 00:26:19,649
You don't have to do that

364
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:23,319
if it's because my feelings
are making you uncomfortable.

365
00:26:26,406 --> 00:26:27,657
I live

366
00:26:28,574 --> 00:26:29,701
with a guy right now.

367
00:26:31,828 --> 00:26:33,496
He's a really nice guy.

368
00:26:34,997 --> 00:26:37,500
So there's no need for you to worry.

369
00:26:39,669 --> 00:26:41,879
I won't get all clingy.

370
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:49,387
Speak of the devil.

371
00:26:50,722 --> 00:26:52,640
I'll see you tomorrow, sir.

372
00:27:09,282 --> 00:27:10,408
What's this about?

373
00:27:12,618 --> 00:27:13,703
Sorry.

374
00:27:14,454 --> 00:27:16,372
I used you for something.

375
00:27:16,456 --> 00:27:17,832
- Was that a guy?
- It's a secret.

376
00:27:18,374 --> 00:27:20,460
What do you want for dinner?
My treat.

377
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:22,503
Why does everyone have a secret?

378
00:27:22,587 --> 00:27:25,339
- Who else has a secret?
- That's my secret, okay?

379
00:27:40,396 --> 00:27:43,024
Doesn't that clear up

380
00:27:43,399 --> 00:27:44,692
what our relationship was?

381
00:27:45,443 --> 00:27:47,820
Doesn't a kiss make it official?

382
00:27:48,821 --> 00:27:51,699
Do you two kiss someone
you're not dating?

383
00:27:52,116 --> 00:27:54,660
Am I the old-fashioned one here?

384
00:27:55,578 --> 00:27:59,123
I mean, if you kiss someone,
doesn't that mean

385
00:27:59,207 --> 00:28:03,169
you have a kind of relationship
that you should be responsible for?

386
00:28:03,503 --> 00:28:04,837
Yes, sure.

387
00:28:05,838 --> 00:28:08,508
But according to Mr. Do...

388
00:28:09,675 --> 00:28:10,968
We kissed?

389
00:28:12,345 --> 00:28:15,640
Now that I think about it,
maybe we did.

390
00:28:16,224 --> 00:28:17,725
I must've been too drunk.

391
00:28:18,559 --> 00:28:21,562
That could also mean
how insignificant it was to me.

392
00:28:22,063 --> 00:28:23,856
She wouldn't stop hitting on me

393
00:28:23,940 --> 00:28:25,358
so while we were drunk...

394
00:28:26,067 --> 00:28:27,276
You know what I mean.

395
00:28:30,655 --> 00:28:34,242
I'm old enough to know how things are

396
00:28:35,368 --> 00:28:36,577
and I'm not stupid.

397
00:28:37,245 --> 00:28:40,122
A momentary mistake
and an emotional connection?

398
00:28:40,206 --> 00:28:43,417
I can definitely make
the distinction very clearly.

399
00:28:46,379 --> 00:28:47,588
You're right.

400
00:28:48,798 --> 00:28:51,092
They're different. I'm not...

401
00:28:51,843 --> 00:28:54,136
You're not old-fashioned, Ms. So.

402
00:28:54,220 --> 00:28:57,014
We know enough
to be able to tell the difference.

403
00:28:57,098 --> 00:28:58,891
Yes, that's it.

404
00:28:59,392 --> 00:29:01,102
What, a mistake?

405
00:29:01,936 --> 00:29:04,730
He can't remember the kiss?
Does he have amnesia?

406
00:29:04,814 --> 00:29:06,816
Did the kiss happen
with only one person?

407
00:29:06,899 --> 00:29:08,276
Why is everything one-sided?

408
00:29:08,359 --> 00:29:10,528
I haven't made sense of it
at all yet.

409
00:29:10,611 --> 00:29:13,030
The other person concluded
like it was nothing.

410
00:29:13,114 --> 00:29:14,365
Right?

411
00:29:14,699 --> 00:29:17,451
So what? It doesn't change anything.

412
00:29:18,411 --> 00:29:20,580
Not all people who kiss are dating.

413
00:29:20,830 --> 00:29:23,332
In some countries,
a kiss is just a greeting.

414
00:29:24,125 --> 00:29:25,418
Do I have to

415
00:29:26,544 --> 00:29:28,296
marry someone just because we kissed?

416
00:29:32,049 --> 00:29:34,385
<i>A kiss definitely makes it official.</i>

417
00:29:35,595 --> 00:29:37,305
You kiss because you're dating

418
00:29:37,388 --> 00:29:38,890
and you date because you kissed.

419
00:29:39,265 --> 00:29:40,766
Our ancestors back in the day

420
00:29:40,850 --> 00:29:44,437
had to take responsibility
and marry someone they talked to.

421
00:29:44,520 --> 00:29:46,147
How far back in time are you going?

422
00:29:46,439 --> 00:29:49,400
These days, you sleep before you date
and go to bed first before going out.

423
00:29:49,692 --> 00:29:50,735
Sleep before what?

424
00:29:50,818 --> 00:29:52,945
You sleep with the partner first
before you start dating them.

425
00:29:53,321 --> 00:29:56,073
And you take someone to bed first
before taking them out.

426
00:29:57,491 --> 00:29:59,994
But aren't kisses a bit different?

427
00:30:00,202 --> 00:30:02,830
There's an old film
called <i>Pretty Woman.</i>

428
00:30:03,414 --> 00:30:05,207
In that film, Julia Roberts

429
00:30:05,291 --> 00:30:08,461
does just about everything
with Richard Gere

430
00:30:09,503 --> 00:30:12,131
but says,
"I don't kiss on the mouth."

431
00:30:13,007 --> 00:30:15,509
Why? Because kissing

432
00:30:15,593 --> 00:30:18,012
is more emotionally charged
than sleeping with someone.

433
00:30:18,679 --> 00:30:21,390
I don't particularly like Mr. Do

434
00:30:21,474 --> 00:30:23,726
but I believe
people can make drunken mistakes.

435
00:30:24,352 --> 00:30:29,065
I mean, getting physical
doesn't always equal a relationship.

436
00:30:29,148 --> 00:30:30,191
I don't know.

437
00:30:30,441 --> 00:30:32,318
We'll have to figure out
the situation before and after

438
00:30:32,401 --> 00:30:34,362
but what bothers me
is the fact that Mr. Do lied.

439
00:30:34,445 --> 00:30:38,115
It's the proof that shows
their kiss must've been significant.

440
00:30:38,199 --> 00:30:41,327
If it really meant nothing,
and he has a clear conscience

441
00:30:41,410 --> 00:30:42,453
he should've admitted to it.

442
00:30:43,204 --> 00:30:44,330
Hey, you're right.

443
00:30:44,956 --> 00:30:46,874
<i>That's true. At times</i>

444
00:30:47,583 --> 00:30:50,044
<i>the truth is hidden between the lies.</i>

445
00:30:51,754 --> 00:30:53,381
- Ms. Joo!
- Goodness.

446
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:56,467
We put this together for you

447
00:30:56,550 --> 00:30:58,010
so make sure
you smooth things over with her.

448
00:30:58,094 --> 00:30:59,887
Kiss up to her and humor her.

449
00:30:59,971 --> 00:31:02,014
- Goodness. This way, please.
- You're all here.

450
00:31:04,141 --> 00:31:05,518
I'll just sit here.

451
00:31:05,601 --> 00:31:07,561
But I set up everything for you

452
00:31:07,645 --> 00:31:08,854
and warmed up the seat.

453
00:31:11,232 --> 00:31:13,067
I see. All right, then.

454
00:31:13,150 --> 00:31:14,527
This way, please.

455
00:31:20,157 --> 00:31:21,993
And a new glass for you.

456
00:31:22,076 --> 00:31:23,369
- Thank you.
- Sure.

457
00:31:27,832 --> 00:31:28,958
Mr. Noh.

458
00:31:29,458 --> 00:31:31,836
What are you waiting for?
She's here. Pour her a drink.

459
00:31:42,388 --> 00:31:44,724
What were you all chatting about?

460
00:31:44,807 --> 00:31:47,601
I saw a few of you
giving a whole speech as I walked in.

461
00:31:47,685 --> 00:31:49,103
It was this.

462
00:31:49,979 --> 00:31:52,982
Ms. Joo.
Kissing equals dating, right?

463
00:31:55,484 --> 00:31:56,485
What?

464
00:32:00,948 --> 00:32:01,991
What do you mean?

465
00:32:07,872 --> 00:32:10,332
You were talking about Mr. Do!

466
00:32:10,958 --> 00:32:14,128
Why are you discussing work
at a team dinner? You workaholics!

467
00:32:14,837 --> 00:32:16,672
Forget that.
Let's talk about something else.

468
00:32:16,756 --> 00:32:18,382
Why? It was just getting fun.

469
00:32:18,841 --> 00:32:21,510
It's not fun to talk about work
while drinking.

470
00:32:22,386 --> 00:32:25,014
- Now, why don't we make a toast?
- Sure.

471
00:32:25,097 --> 00:32:27,349
Fill up your glasses.

472
00:32:27,641 --> 00:32:29,143
Thank you.

473
00:32:29,226 --> 00:32:32,146
For the workaholics
of Audit Team Three.

474
00:32:32,229 --> 00:32:34,648
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

475
00:32:47,495 --> 00:32:49,705
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine. I'm okay.

476
00:32:50,289 --> 00:32:52,958
So do you want to grab
one more drink?

477
00:32:53,417 --> 00:32:56,587
Your team should let loose
without me in round two

478
00:32:56,670 --> 00:32:58,089
so you can talk behind my back.

479
00:32:58,172 --> 00:33:00,132
Goodness, don't say
something like that.

480
00:33:00,216 --> 00:33:03,177
All of us, especially Mr. Noh

481
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:06,764
adore and respect you so much,
Ms. Joo.

482
00:33:06,847 --> 00:33:12,311
He's right. Ms. Joo, you are
the coolest boss in the world.

483
00:33:12,394 --> 00:33:13,687
He's drunk.

484
00:33:13,896 --> 00:33:15,147
Mr. Baek.

485
00:33:15,231 --> 00:33:17,525
You once said I wasn't good enough

486
00:33:17,608 --> 00:33:19,944
and that I should
draw the line for the team.

487
00:33:20,027 --> 00:33:22,905
Didn't you look at me like this
and get angry at me?

488
00:33:23,322 --> 00:33:26,575
Well, back then,
I didn't know any better.

489
00:33:26,659 --> 00:33:29,328
But Ms. Joo, you really know

490
00:33:29,411 --> 00:33:31,747
how to draw the perfect line!

491
00:33:36,001 --> 00:33:37,128
Mr. Noh.

492
00:33:37,503 --> 00:33:40,381
You should be good to Ms. Joo, okay?

493
00:33:42,508 --> 00:33:45,094
Goodness.
It's time for you to go home.

494
00:33:45,177 --> 00:33:46,470
- My gosh.
- Careful.

495
00:33:46,846 --> 00:33:49,557
All right, then.
We should call it a night.

496
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:51,225
Okay. Wait, Mr. Noh.

497
00:33:51,308 --> 00:33:54,061
You should grab a cab for Ms. Joo.
It's quite late.

498
00:33:54,145 --> 00:33:56,063
- No, it's all right.
- It's not all right!

499
00:33:56,147 --> 00:33:58,065
Make sure you grab it for her.
Do that, okay?

500
00:33:58,149 --> 00:34:00,526
- See you tomorrow!
- See you tomorrow!

501
00:34:00,609 --> 00:34:03,487
- Sure. Have a safe trip back home.
- Mr. Moo.

502
00:34:04,738 --> 00:34:07,032
What? No, I can't do that.
It's too late.

503
00:34:07,116 --> 00:34:08,659
- The night is still young.
- No.

504
00:34:10,077 --> 00:34:12,163
They think I hate you, don't they?

505
00:34:13,455 --> 00:34:15,416
You have the best teammates.

506
00:34:16,375 --> 00:34:17,751
They're good people.

507
00:34:19,962 --> 00:34:21,172
So...

508
00:34:23,382 --> 00:34:24,842
it sounds like you don't hate me.

509
00:34:46,989 --> 00:34:49,158
Hey, there's my cab.
See you tomorrow.

510
00:34:51,076 --> 00:34:54,246
VACANT

511
00:34:56,457 --> 00:34:58,542
- To AL Tower, please.
- Sure.

512
00:35:04,882 --> 00:35:07,051
- Sir, please start driving.
- What are you doing?

513
00:35:10,012 --> 00:35:11,722
It's late, so I thought
I'd bring you home.

